## ⚙️ Environment Variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and adjust the values for your environment. Application settings map to the fields in `core/config.py`:

| Variable | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | Environment name used in application startup logs. |
| `DEBUG` | `false` | Enables FastAPI debug mode when set to `true`. |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Root logging level. |
| `UVICORN_HOST` | `0.0.0.0` | Configured Uvicorn bind host. |
| `UVICORN_PORT` | `8000` | Configured Uvicorn bind port. |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | `["http://localhost:3000","http://localhost:8000"]` | JSON array of allowed CORS origins. |
| `CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS` | `true` | Whether CORS requests may include credentials. |
| `APP_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Host passed by the `just run-dev` recipe. |
| `APP_PORT` | `8000` | Host port used by `just run-dev` and Docker Compose. |
{% if include_docker and include_network %}| `NETWORK_NAME` | `{{ network_slug }}` | Docker Compose network name. |
{% endif %}

`APP_HOST`, `APP_PORT`, and `NETWORK_NAME` configure the development command or Docker Compose; they are not fields on the Pydantic `Settings` model. The Copier questionnaire options (such as project name, author, and architecture choices) are generation-time inputs and do not belong in `.env`.

